def search(nums, target):
    left, right = 0, len(nums) - 1

    while left <= right:
        mid = (left + right) // 2

        if nums[mid] == target:
            return mid
        elif nums[mid] < target:
            left = mid + 1
        else:
            right = mid - 1

    return -1
```
This function implements binary search by repeatedly dividing the search interval in half. It checks if the middle element is the target, and adjusts the search range accordingly until the target is found or the range is exhausted. The time complexity is O(log n) as required.
